User-visible changes to windetect in between releases:

--- 24-Dec-2020  Release 1.0b1 ---

* Corrected initial notification by windetect.test
* Some documentation improvements (textual and lay-out of the PDF document)

--- 24-Feb-2021  Release 1.0.0 ---

* (enhancement) new command "instrument", which facilitates configuration
  of the internal detection mechanism.
* (enhancement) remove implicit default instrumentation upon switching
  detection on. This introduces an

      *** INCOMPATIBILITY ***

  with previous releases. Instrumenting the GUI is left to the user as an
  explicit programming step, employing the new "instrument" command.
* (enhancement) refrain from reporting virtual crossings
* (enhancement) new option -wsrespite to address timing issues with the
  windowing system when using a zero reporting delay, thereby making the
  detection of the new pointer window much more accurate.
* (enhancement) adapt to Tk invoking binding scripts for events with detail
  field NotifyInferior (since Tk8.6.15)
* (enhancement) adapt to several incompatibilities introduced by Tcl9.0.0
* (bug fix) correct initial reporting when detection is activated.
* (bug fix) correct reporting of the new pointer window upon destruction of
  the old pointer window when using a zero reporting delay.
* (bug fix) correct reporting of the new pointer window when moving the mouse
  pointer outside a grabbed toplevel window.
* (bug fix) correct reporting of the new pointer window upon destruction of
  the old pointer window if a grab is in effect and the mouse pointer is
  outside the grab subtree.
* (bug fix) correct reporting of the new pointer window when a grab is being
  set or released, and the mouse pointer resides outside the grab subtree.
* (bug fix) correct pointer coordinates reported when a grab is being set or
  released.
* (bug fix) correct check for Tk version requirement
* (test enhancement) add unit tests for private event and trace handlers.
* (test enhancement) use a proper test file for gui-integration tests,
  thereby removing the dependency on package tkwintrack.
* (test enhancement) make gui-integration tests insensitive to variability
  among windowing systems and window managers w.r.t. timeliness of event
  notifications, thereby considerably speeding up test execution.
* (test enhancement) add various inspection facilities to the test scripts.
* Substantial documentation enhancements, especially regarding instrumentation,
  limitations, testing and windowing system particulars.

--- 17-Sep-2024  Release 2.0.0 ---

* (doc fix) correct Tk release nr. where invoking binding scripts for events
  with detail field NotifyInferior was fixed (#5)
* (test fix) remove inappropriate constraint from tests pw_destroy-4.[12] (#6)

--- 22-Sep-2024  Release 2.0.1 ---
